From 9dc1c90ec09899dad3c3e3d84e565215c81b9a8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 23:05:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix stuck 'call already in progress', chat panel showing
 behind a call, and missing ringback tone

1. 'A call is already in progress in this conversation' getting stuck
   permanently: an 'accepted' call had no way to expire on its own if
   one side disconnected without a clean hangup (closed tab, lost
   network, phone locked, browser crash - beforeunload/sendBeacon
   doesn't fire reliably in any of those). Added
   database/migration_chat_calls_activity.sql (ChatCalls.last_activity_at)
   - refreshed for free every time either side polls call_status or
     call_ice_candidates (already happening every ~1.2s while a call is
     up), and an 'accepted' call nobody has polled in 20s is now
     force-closed the next time any call action runs the existing
     stale-call sweep.

2. Chat messages/panel showing behind the call screen: .pos-chat-panel
   and .pos-chat-toggle were z-index 1091, one point HIGHER than
   .pos-call-overlay's 1090, so the open chat panel rendered on top of
   the call. Raised the call overlay/incoming-call banner above both,
   and belt-and-suspenders: the chat panel and floating toggle button
   are now explicitly hidden while a call is active and restored after
   (only if the panel was actually open before the call started).

3. No ringtone for the caller while ringing (only the callee's incoming
   banner had one) - added a ringback tone that starts the moment the
   call starts ringing and stops as soon as the status changes (answered,
   declined, missed, or ended).
